WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.302
Tonight, Senate Minority Leader

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.003
Mitch McConnell

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.471
speaking out about a health scare

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:05.271
earlier today

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.407
where he froze for about 30 seconds

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:08.775
during a news conference.

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.478
Here's what he just told reporters

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:14.681
The president called to check on me.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.683
I told him I got sandbagged.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.052
Oh, nice. How are you feeling now, sir?

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:20.086
How are you feeling now?

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:20.553
Fine.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.988
Have you seen a doctor or are you going.

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:23.957
Any idea what happened?

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:25.325
Well, any idea what happened?

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:26.126
I'm fine.

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.728
That's dehydrated.

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.964
Got to watch those sandbags Inspector.

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:31.865
So,

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:35.368
did you talk to a doctor today?

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:35.902
Folks, we're good.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:36.836
Thank you.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.206
Sandbag, of course, is a reference

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:41.508
to Joe Biden

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.777
right at his commencement address

00:00:43.777 --> 00:00:45.612
that McConnell was making.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:46.046
But here's

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:49.516
what happened to McConnell earlier today.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.652
We're on a path to finishing the NDAA

00:00:54.788 --> 00:00:55.555
This week

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.757
has been good bipartisan cooperation

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:18.111
and a string of stuff.

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.682
When are you going

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.484
to make

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:25.652
this change?

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:26.553
Anything else you want to say?

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.288
I'm sure to go back to you.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:29.355
Do you want to say anything else

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.423
to the press?

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:32.959
Correct.

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:35.595
I'll take you.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:36.529
Let's go back to you.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:37.664
Go ahead, John.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.435
Be glad you

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:45.505
So this is the we're coming up

00:01:45.505 --> 00:01:49.142
on the one year anniversary, the IRA.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:49.442
All right.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.245
So it is obviously hard to watch.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.379
It was a press conference

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:54.214
OUTFRONT now, Dr.

00:01:54.214 --> 00:01:55.315
Jonathan Reiner, CNN

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:56.816
medical analyst and cardiologist

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:58.618
who advised the White House medical team

00:01:58.618 --> 00:02:00.220
under President George W Bush.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.621
Along with Dana Bash, our chief

00:02:01.621 --> 00:02:02.622
political correspondent,

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.190
anchor of Inside Politics.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.758
And a long time

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:06.860
you know, you've covered McConnell,

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:07.961
obviously, for many years, Dana.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:08.394
So Dr.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.429
Reiner, an aide,

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.396
says McConnell

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.231
felt lightheaded

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:13.266
and stepped away for a moment.

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:13.833
But as I said,

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.802
that video is hard to watch.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.803
He stares off.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:19.339
He's not blinking more than 20 seconds

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.141
pass. Obviously, this is

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.743
a crucial individual.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.678
What stands out to you?

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:26.846
Well, first of all, you're right.

00:02:26.846 --> 00:02:27.614
It's very difficult

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.883
to watch somebody have an acute event.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:30.350
And I think

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:31.684
what Senator McConnell had

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:34.120
was an acute neurologic event.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.121
It's important to remember

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:36.389
that he had a concussion

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.290
four months ago,

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.224
which is basically

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.226
a traumatic brain injury.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.228
And about 10% of people

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.663
who need to be hospitalized

00:02:43.663 --> 00:02:45.431
for a traumatic brain injury

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.400
like Senator McConnell

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:47.934
will suffer

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:51.070
from a post-concussion seizure.

00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:52.872
And I think that's what we watched.

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.974
The the staring straight ahead

00:02:55.341 --> 00:02:56.643
was really very,

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.710
very stark

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.213
and actually very difficult to watch.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:01.948
And I think he had the kind of seizure

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.950
that is sometimes called an absent

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:05.618
seizure, seizure.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:07.587
I was glad to see him recover

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.722
and be able to talk to the press

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.823
about 10 minutes later,

00:03:10.823 --> 00:03:11.891
and then this evening,

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.426
he even looked better.

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.661
So that's good news.

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.029
But to me, that's what it looked like.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.564
It looked like he had a seizure.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:19.432
How serious is an event like that?

00:03:19.432 --> 00:03:20.133
Dr..

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:20.934
Well,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:21.467
the other

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.203
striking thing about watching

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.671
Senator McConnell

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:27.207
is that he looks so frail now.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.276
You know, until about a year ago,

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.245
until about six months ago,

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.079
Senator McConnell

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.215
was this really vibrant presence.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.816
And now he looked,

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.418
you know, almost almost deflated

00:03:38.418 --> 00:03:39.652
and very, very fragile.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:40.386
And his

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:42.755
his injury has really taken a toll.

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:45.525
And that's what happens when older people

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:46.392
Senator McConnell is.

00:03:46.392 --> 00:03:47.527
81 years old

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:48.094
when older

00:03:48.094 --> 00:03:50.296
people have a traumatic injury and a fall

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:53.233
This is sometimes the consequence

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:54.167
they come out of it,

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.868
maybe not the same person.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:56.636
Jenny, you've covered

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:57.570
McConnell for years.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.171
What are you hearing

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:00.240
from your sources tonight?

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:04.544
I spoke to somebody who spoke

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:06.879
privately to the Republican leader

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.515
not long after that incident.

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.518
He insisted in private, just as he has

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.153
done, along with his aides

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.722
in public, that he was fine.

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:16.656
He did, as Dr.

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:17.423
Rinder said,

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:18.725
come back to the microphones.

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.193
He kept his schedule

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:21.794
for the rest of the day.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:23.763
They might even be in votes tonight.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:24.764
They're waiting to see if there's

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:27.100
a deal on the defense bill.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:29.202
And I was told that he has a dinner,

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.170
that he is still intending

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.573
to attend this evening.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:36.709
But you can definitely see the fear,

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:39.779
obviously, not just for Senator McConnell

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:41.347
but the Republican leaders

00:04:41.347 --> 00:04:43.549
who are standing around him.

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.450
They obviously wanted

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.318
to give him a moment

00:04:45.318 --> 00:04:46.686
because they didn't know what

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.021
was happening.

00:04:48.021 --> 00:04:49.622
But then they finally realized

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.823
this is a time

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.157
when we need

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:54.127
to move him away from the cameras.

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:55.795
Yes, he

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:56.796
he is older

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.231
and he has been vibrant,

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:00.366
but he is also somebody who

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.068
suffered from polio

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.970
when he was a young boy.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.539
And he is not

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:07.073
somebody who

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:08.875
has always skipped down the hallway.

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:09.809
So yes,

00:05:09.809 --> 00:05:11.844
we see a bit of a difference there,

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.447
but not a huge difference,

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.516
at least to the untrained eye,

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:17.817
compared to what Dr.

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.419
Reiner would see and Dr.

00:05:19.419 --> 00:05:19.986
Reiner McConnell

00:05:19.986 --> 00:05:21.187
did continue his work day

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:22.555
after the incident, as you said.

00:05:22.555 --> 00:05:24.390
You know, you're glad that he did that.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.091
Dana mentions

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:27.060
he voted and maybe votes even tonight,

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.561
she just indicated.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:29.162
But you heard

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.630
McConnell asked by a few reporters

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.731
whether he went to see a doctor.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:32.432
He didn't answer.

00:05:32.432 --> 00:05:33.066
I mean, obviously,

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.701
that doesn't mean he didn't

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.436
have you know, I'm sure a call was made.

00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:38.738
I can't imagine one was not.

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:40.406
But but again, in the context

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.709
of what you're describing this,

00:05:42.709 --> 00:05:45.044
what you think it was,

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:46.946
is this something that would, you know,

00:05:46.946 --> 00:05:50.583
impact his ability to do his job or not

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:52.985
or have more serious consequences?

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:54.253
Well, I

00:05:54.253 --> 00:05:54.954
think it speaks

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.756
to the intensity of the injury

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:58.057
that he had in March.

00:05:58.057 --> 00:05:58.624
And, you know,

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:01.060
he was in the hospital for several days,

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.195
and then he went to rehab

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:03.663
for a couple of weeks.

00:06:03.663 --> 00:06:04.731
And he didn't return,

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:06.632
I think, to the to the Senate

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:07.934
for about six weeks.

00:06:07.934 --> 00:06:10.403
And that really is a long absence

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:11.938
after a concussion.

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:13.306
So I think we really know

00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:16.542
that he had a quite a severe injury

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:18.411
back in March.

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.880
But as for how he would be evaluated now,

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.948
I think it depends on

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:24.417
whether he's had this episode before.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:27.487
If this episode has happened in the weeks

00:06:27.487 --> 00:06:28.988
and months after the event

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:31.124
and it's been investigated already,

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:32.492
which would typically be

00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:35.528
with a full neurologic exam and scans, CT

00:06:35.661 --> 00:06:37.096
scan and MRI scan,

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:37.630
then there might

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.832
not be any reason to repeat it now.

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:41.134
But if this is the first time

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:42.902
he has had an episode like this

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:45.104
where he stopped in mid-sentence

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:48.040
staring into space for almost a minute,

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.076
then this would really require

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:52.678
a full neurologic exam and

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:56.082
imaging, you know, today.

00:06:56.082 --> 00:06:56.616
So Dana,

00:06:56.616 --> 00:06:59.152
what does this mean for his future

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:03.156
Well, in the short term,

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:06.225
nothing, if you believe what he said.

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:07.794
Obviously making a point

00:07:07.794 --> 00:07:10.263
to go out to the cameras to make a joke

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:12.565
after he spoke to the president,

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:14.834
as you said, the sandbag joke.

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:17.503
That was kind of a 80 year old.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:20.039
81 year old to an 80 year old

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:21.240
Something really bad happened

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.275
in front of the cameras.

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:24.177
Very inside joke.

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:26.679
But the fact that he's trying to

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:28.047
be feeling now

00:07:28.047 --> 00:07:30.216
and his aides are trying to intentionally

00:07:31.117 --> 00:07:33.419
say that he's okay

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:36.622
it means that he has no intention

00:07:36.622 --> 00:07:38.024
of changing anything,

00:07:38.024 --> 00:07:39.292
at least in the near term.

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:42.228
Look, just by reelection

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:44.597
numbers he's not up until 20, 26

00:07:44.597 --> 00:07:46.299
so he's got several years

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:49.202
and he is absolutely has been determined

00:07:49.735 --> 00:07:50.636
to try to win back

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:51.270
enough seats

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:52.405
finally in the United States

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:54.440
Senate to become majority leader again.

00:07:54.440 --> 00:07:55.908
And I haven't gotten any indication

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:57.510
that that changed today.

00:07:57.510 --> 00:07:57.910
All right.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.245
Thank you both very much.

00:07:59.245 --> 00:07:59.979
I appreciate it.

